{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / immutable basis\nExactly 31 bloated prose blocks are confirmed across 18 paths. They comprise 27 leading owner docstrings and 4 ordinary full-line comment regions with 7,097 base words under the receipt tokenizer. Condense repetition, obvious narration, duplicated explanation, and obsolete change history while retaining current non-obvious contracts.\n\nBefore citations and word counts use `origin/main@d6669496cae441fc8381b5ee6de21a3993defd84`. A path-scoped comparison through `88c90f8b5abf4a80be3b1289d7719d6e03e29684` found zero overlap. The original remediation is fixed at Gerrit change 2967 merged SHA `914a8a1da121497c7ade065ec84564633603b4a1`. Its parent differs from the frozen base only by the two legitimate `_NON_MUTATING` census entries `get_local_id_map` and `_issue_local_id_property`. A second comment-only change corrects documentation-policy findings on current `origin/main`. Verification proves the original and corrective diffs separately and then audits the final 31-block inventory.\n\n## Boundary and immutable oracle\nBelow, `R` means `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler`. `D:<qualified-owner>` identifies only that owner's leading string docstring; `C:<anchor>@Lx-y` identifies one contiguous base comment region. Edit only these IDs. Every block must shrink and state current rationale/constraints; preserve cited literals and behavioral oracles.\n\nParse both review changes with `ast.parse(..., type_comments=True)`. Replace only allowlisted leading docstring values, normalize only `ast.TypeIgnore.lineno`, and require exact attribute-free AST equality for each parent/final pair. The original-change oracle separately requires the frozen-base-to-original-parent scoped diff to contain exactly the two declared census additions. The corrective oracle restricts every `HEAD^..HEAD` hunk to the 31 allowlisted blocks. Tokenize independently to preserve directive and shebang text plus inline or next-statement attachment. The final inventory compares immutable before blocks with completion `HEAD`, requires every block to remain shorter, and applies `docs/documentation-policy.md`. Runtime strings, inline comments, unlisted prose, and executable syntax remain exact.\n\n## Scope — 31 editable blocks\n- `R/test_cloud_rate_limit_sweep_heldout.py` (1) — `D:module`; preserve the four 429 boundary classes, per-member mutation/nonmutation census, duplicate-write safety, and anti-drift contract.\n- `R/test_cloud_unassign_6a74.py` (1) — `D:module`; preserve positive `accountId:null` unassign, no empty ACLI assignment, and deterministic seams.\n- `R/test_dc_backend_characterization.py` (3) — `D:module`; `C:\"MUTATION LEDGER — every pin...\"@L57-129`; `C:\"AC3 — the SHARED OutboundFieldMapper...\"@L391-402`. Preserve DC value pins/divergences, literal mutation results, and the fit-not-ordering boundary.\n- `R/test_dc_comment_ceiling_049e.py` (1) — `D:module`; preserve raised/lowered/zero/default ceilings, local literal expectations, and separation from description fitting.\n- `R/test_dc_create_field_translation_18a5.py` (1) — `D:module`; preserve bridge-to-Jira field translation, object wrapping, null omission, summary fit, and no bridge-schema leakage.\n- `R/test_dc_epic_link_parent_39c1.py` (4) — `D:module`, `D:_FakeClient`, `D:test_epic_parent_on_a_non_subtask_is_written_as_an_epic_link`, `D:test_the_emit_gate_and_dc_apply_now_overlap`; preserve field discovery/cache, Epic Link versus sub-task paths, decline behavior, and intersecting gates.\n- `R/test_dc_force_reindex.py` (1) — `D:module`; preserve issue-id POST, credential safety, and best-effort/no-op accelerator behavior.\n- `R/test_dc_inbound_epic_link_9bb9.py` (1) — `D:_FakeClient`; preserve the search/fields fake shape and field-discovery failure axis.\n- `R/test_dc_live_oracles_discriminate_5200.py` (6) — `D:module`, `D:test_the_writer_emits_the_COLON_label_form_and_nothing_emits_the_hyphen`, `D:_truncating_paged_search`, `D:test_the_old_precondition_fails_on_the_very_defect_it_disclaimed`, `C:\"GAP 4 — row 12 OUTBOUND...\"@L423-434`, `D:test_dc_set_parent_USES_A_DIFFERENT_PATH_for_the_non_subtask_case`; preserve writer provenance, old-pager discrimination, and distinct parent paths.\n- `R/test_dc_outbound_status_routing_5200.py` (2) — `D:module`, `D:test_the_dc_transport_never_edits_status_as_a_field`; preserve transition routing, exclusion from field edits, co-submitted fields, and narrow soft failures.\n- `R/test_dc_pat_required_heldout.py` (1) — `D:module`; preserve fail-closed PAT security at client construction and total settings resolution for Protocol checks.\n- `R/test_dc_rate_limit_retry_heldout.py` (1) — `D:module`; preserve opt-in read retries, `Retry-After`, bounded delay, and no blanket mutation replay.\n- `R/test_dc_send_path_comment_fit.py` (1) — `D:module`; preserve marker-safe send fitting, configured ceiling, and next-pass dedup convergence.\n- `R/test_dc_subtask_parent_readback_1a9f.py` (1) — `D:module`; preserve 204 accept-and-ignore readback, unrepresentable classification, and future-compatible success.\n- `R/test_dc_transition_by_status_heldout.py` (1) — `D:module`; preserve destination-status lookup, exact-name precedence, ambiguity rejection, and missing-destination tolerance.\n- `R/test_dc_transport_pagination_heldout.py` (2) — `D:module`, `C:\"OFFSET-STALL...\"@L317-345`; preserve one pager for all readers, server-capped short pages, and loud repeated-offset failure.\n- `R/test_dc_unassign_751e.py` (2) — `D:module`, `D:test_empty_outbound_assignee_actually_unassigns`; preserve the `None` versus `-1`/empty vendor contract and resulting-field oracle.\n- `R/test_error_taxonomy.py` (1) — `D:module`; preserve canonical exception identity/MRO and chained retry causes.\n\n## Protected exclusions and consumers\nAll 253 other owner-docstring/full-line-comment blocks are excluded. Concise examples include `test_a_real_pat_builds_a_client` (8 words), `_Recorder` (9), and `_backend` (9). Longer structural/per-test explanations such as `_is_pure_transport_facade`, the anti-drift/pagination teeth, transition controls, and non-string mapper oracle are load-bearing and remain exact. Preserve 22 directive tokens with attachment: 5 arg-type ignores, 5 attr-defined ignores, 4 assignment ignores, 5 E402 noqas, 1 PT008 noqa, and 2 no-cover pragmas.\n\nPytest collects every impacted module; `scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py` is the prose-policy consumer. Source-reading tests inspect production files, not these editable blocks. No targeted `__doc__`, `inspect.getdoc`, doctest, or pydoc consumer was found.\n\n## Independent review receipt\nA reviewer who did not author the prose change must post exactly 31 leaf-linked TSV rows:\n`path<TAB>block-id<TAB>before-full-SHA:lines<TAB>final-full-SHA:lines<TAB>preserved-contract-or-consumer<TAB>before-words<TAB>after-words<TAB>directives-exact<TAB>semantic-preservation<TAB>bloat-removal<TAB>reviewer-session`\n\nBefore citations use `d6669496cae441fc8381b5ee6de21a3993defd84`; final citations use the full final SHA. Every after count is lower and all three verdict columns are `PASS`. Missing, duplicate, or extra rows block closure.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Across the original and corrective reviews, only the 31 allowlisted base blocks change.\n- [ ] Every edited block is shorter and current.\n- [ ] The fixed original SHA and the corrective `HEAD^..HEAD` pair each pass normalized AST and directive equality, while frozen-base drift before the original change is exactly the two declared census entries.\n- [ ] Runtime strings remain AST-identical.\n- [ ] Directive/shebang text and attachment remain exact.\n- [ ] Original SHA `914a8a1da121497c7ade065e